IMPORT prelude

-- Charities Act 1994 (Singapore) -- institutions of a public character (IPCs) and Sector Administrators (Part 9, ss 40 to 42),
-- and the offence of holding out as an IPC (s 49).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 April 2023), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CA1994.txt. Section numbers are the body's (ss 40, 41, 42, 49; formerly ss 40A, 40B, 40C,
-- 43A, as the bracketed margin notes show).
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0292 (Haziq scenario, event h072, 2051): "A newly registered charity
-- wishes donations to it to be tax-deductible. What status must it hold, who grants it, and on what conditions?"
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the approval criteria themselves, the period of approval, extension and revocation procedure, the rules on
-- constitution amendments, the use of donations, tax deduction receipts and donation records, and appeals from Sector
-- Administrators -- the Act leaves all of these to regulations under s 42(1), which were not retrieved; the Gazette notices
-- designating each Sector Administrator's sector (s 40 "sector"); which written laws deem an institution an IPC (s 40(b));
-- s 42(4) remission is taken as a given amount, with no rule for how much the Commissioner remits; s 42(6) (Limitation Act);
-- the tax deduction itself (Income Tax Act 1947 s 37(3)(c) to (f) and (3A) to (3G)) -- pointed to, not computed.
-- (The s 42 regulations -- Rg 5, the IPC Regulations -- are now encoded in cha-ipc-regulations.l4.)
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Charities Act 1994 -- institutions of a public character`

§§ `40 -- what an institution of a public character is`

-- s 40: "'institution of a public character' means a registered charity or an exempt charity in Singapore --
--   (a) that is approved as an institution of a public character by the Minister, Commissioner or any Sector Administrator on
--       the application of the charity; or
--   (b) which is deemed as an institution of a public character under any written law".
-- s 2: "'exempt charity' means a charity specified in the Schedule".
DECLARE `Charity status` IS ONE OF
    `a registered charity`
    `an exempt charity`
    `an unregistered charity`
    `not a charity`

DECLARE Approver IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `the Commissioner`
    `a Sector Administrator`
    `the Comptroller of Income Tax`
    `no one`

GIVEN `the approver` IS AN Approver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an approving authority under section 40` IF
    CONSIDER `the approver`
    WHEN `the Minister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Sector Administrator` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the status` IS A `Charity status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a registered or exempt charity` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `a registered charity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an exempt charity` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the status` IS A `Charity status`
      `the charity applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by` IS AN Approver
      `deemed an IPC under written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the institution is an IPC` IF
    `is a registered or exempt charity` `the status`
    AND (    (`the charity applied` AND `is an approving authority under section 40` `approved by`)
          OR `deemed an IPC under written law`)

-- The Act itself states no approval criteria. s 42(1): "The Minister may make regulations to provide for -- (a) the manner and
-- criteria to be adopted -- (i) for the approval of institutions of a public character; and (ii) for the extension and
-- revocation of the approval granted to institutions of a public character".
GIVETH A STRING
`where the conditions for IPC approval are set` MEANS
    "in regulations made by the Minister under s 42(1)(a); the Act itself sets none"

-- POINTER, NOT COMPUTED. Income Tax Act 1947 s 37(3)(c) (read in subjects/sg/income-tax-act-1947/registers/source-bundle) deducts
-- a multiple of "any donation of money ... to -- (i) the Government; or (ii) any institution of a public character", and its s 2
-- gives "institution of a public character" "the meaning given by the Charities Act 1994". So a donation to a charity can only
-- fall under s 37(3)(c)(ii) if the charity is an IPC in the s 40 sense. Whether a given donation is deductible turns on the
-- Income Tax Act's own conditions (s 37(3B) to (3G)), not encoded here.
GIVEN `the status` IS A `Charity status`
      `the charity applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by` IS AN Approver
      `deemed an IPC under written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `donations to it can be within Income Tax Act s 37(3)(c)(ii)` IF
    `the institution is an IPC` `the status` `the charity applied` `approved by` `deemed an IPC under written law`

§§ `41 -- Sector Administrators`

-- s 41: "The Minister may appoint any person or organisation to be a Sector Administrator for one or more of the following
-- purposes: (a) regulating the administration of charities within the sector; (b) approving institutions as institutions of a
-- public character from among such class or classes of institutions as the Minister or Commissioner may determine;
-- (c) regulating the administration of donations made to institutions of a public character within the sector; (d) exercising
-- such other functions and powers as the Minister may determine."
-- So a Sector Administrator approves IPCs only if appointed for purpose (b), and only from the classes determined for it.
GIVEN `appointed for approving IPCs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charity is in a class determined for that Sector Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Sector Administrator may approve this charity as an IPC` IF
    `appointed for approving IPCs` AND `the charity is in a class determined for that Sector Administrator`

§§ `42 -- regulations, delegation and penalties`

-- s 42(1)(e): regulations may provide for "the delegation by the Commissioner to any Sector Administrator of any of the
-- Commissioner's functions or powers, except those which are exercisable under sections 22, 23, 24, 26, 27 and 31".
GIVEN `section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner's powers under the section may be delegated to a Sector Administrator` IF
    NOT (   `section` EQUALS 22
         OR `section` EQUALS 23
         OR `section` EQUALS 24
         OR `section` EQUALS 26
         OR `section` EQUALS 27
         OR `section` EQUALS 31)

-- s 42(2)(a): for a contravention of the regulations, "where the person is a registered charity or an exempt charity, the
-- Minister, Commissioner or appropriate Sector Administrator may revoke the approval of the person as an institution of a public
-- character". (Only if the regulations so provide -- s 42(2) says the regulations "may provide for" these consequences.)
GIVEN `the status` IS A `Charity status`
      `contravened the IPC regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the IPC approval may be revoked under section 42(2)(a)` IF
    `contravened the IPC regulations` AND `is a registered or exempt charity` `the status`

-- s 42(2)(b) and s 49 carry the same penalty: "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years
-- or ... both and, in the case of a continuing offence, ... a further fine not exceeding $100 for every day or part of a day
-- during which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for an IPC offence` MEANS
    10000 + 100 * `days continuing after conviction`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for an IPC offence` MEANS 3

-- s 42(2)(c): for a contravention "of a regulation relating to the issue of tax deduction receipts which is not an offence under
-- paragraph (b)", a financial penalty "being the higher of the following amounts: (i) $100; (ii) the amount ascertained by the
-- formula 0.4 x the total value of the donations (as determined under section 37(3) of the Income Tax Act 1947) which ought not
-- to be allowed a deduction under section 37(3) of the Income Tax Act 1947 by reason of the contravention, if any."
GIVEN `donations wrongly receipted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax deduction receipt penalty` MEANS
    IF 0.4 * `donations wrongly receipted` GREATER THAN 100
    THEN 0.4 * `donations wrongly receipted`
    ELSE 100

-- s 42(3): the penalty "is recoverable as a debt due to the Government". (4): "The Commissioner may remit or refund the whole or
-- any part". (5): it "must, after deducting any remission or refund under subsection (4), be paid into the Consolidated Fund".
GIVEN `donations wrongly receipted` IS A NUMBER
      `remitted or refunded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount paid into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    IF `remitted or refunded` AT LEAST `the tax deduction receipt penalty` `donations wrongly receipted`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the tax deduction receipt penalty` `donations wrongly receipted` - `remitted or refunded`

-- s 42(7): "Where any Sector Administrator contravenes any regulations made under subsection (1), the Minister may revoke the
-- appointment of the Sector Administrator."
GIVEN `the Sector Administrator contravened the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may revoke the Sector Administrator's appointment` IF
    `the Sector Administrator contravened the regulations`

§§ `49 -- holding out as an IPC`

-- s 49: "Where any institution holds itself out to be a registered charity or an institution of a public character when it is
-- not ... the institution and any person acting or purporting to act on behalf of or for the benefit of the institution, unless
-- the person proves that such holding out by the institution was made without the person's knowledge or consent, shall be guilty
-- of an offence".
GIVEN `holds itself out as an IPC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is in fact an IPC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the institution commits the s 49 offence` IF
    `holds itself out as an IPC` AND (NOT `is in fact an IPC`)

GIVEN `holds itself out as an IPC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is in fact an IPC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts on behalf of the institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proves it was without the person's knowledge or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the s 49 offence` IF
    `the institution commits the s 49 offence` `holds itself out as an IPC` `is in fact an IPC`
    AND `acts on behalf of the institution`
    AND (NOT `proves it was without the person's knowledge or consent`)
